From: Jiahao Xu <xujiahao@cmss.chinamobile.com>
To: Dmitry Torokhov <dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com>
Cc: linux-input@vger.kernel.org, linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org
Subject: [PATCH] Input: cobra - use scnprintf() for the device phys name

cobra_connect() composes the physical path of each port as
"%s/input%d" from gameport->phys into a 32-byte array.  gameport->phys
is a 32-byte string and the port number is an int, so the worst case is
31 + 6 + 10 characters plus the terminator and does not fit.  The
result is informational only and is truncated on these devices today,
which is fine; use scnprintf() so that the helper makes it explicit
that the output is bounded by the buffer.

This also silences the W=1 warning:

  drivers/input/joystick/cobra.c:184:29: warning: '/input' directive
    output may be truncated writing 6 bytes into a region of size
    between 1 and 32 [-Wformat-truncation=]

No functional change.

Signed-off-by: Jiahao Xu <xujiahao@cmss.chinamobile.com>
---
 drivers/input/joystick/cobra.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/joystick/cobra.c b/drivers/input/joystick/cobra.c
index ffa6d49c8..52331a947 100644
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/cobra.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/cobra.c
@@ -180,8 +180,8 @@ static int cobra_connect(struct gameport *gameport, struct gameport_driver *drv)
 			goto fail3;
 		}
 
-		snprintf(cobra->phys[i], sizeof(cobra->phys[i]),
-			 "%s/input%d", gameport->phys, i);
+		scnprintf(cobra->phys[i], sizeof(cobra->phys[i]),
+			  "%s/input%d", gameport->phys, i);
 
 		input_dev->name = "Creative Labs Blaster GamePad Cobra";
 		input_dev->phys = cobra->phys[i];
